  "changelog": {
    "version": "0.2.1",
    "title": "River Client 0.2.1",
    "summary": "River now runs on Linux (experimental), and creative flying can be a lot faster.",
    "items": [
      "River now runs on Linux (experimental): download the tar.gz from riverclient.xyz, extract it and run ./river-client.",
      "On Linux, Java is found in the usual places or downloaded for you, other launchers' profiles are found for importing (Minecraft launcher, Modrinth, Prism, MultiMC and more), and screenshots copy through wl-copy or xclip.",
      "Linux can't update itself yet: when a new version is out, the launcher opens the download page.",
      "Added Creative Fly Speed (Gameplay): fly up to 10x faster in creative mode. It only affects creative, and vanilla speed returns when you leave creative or turn it off."
    ]
  },
  "notes": "River now runs on Linux (experimental), and creative flying can be a lot faster."
